{
  "description": "Where a message's spoilers are, which the client's renderer (features/messages/remarkSpoilers.ts, read through spoilerTree in maskSpoilers.ts) and the server's notification text and email digest (app::message::notification::spoilers) both find alike. content: a message's text. shown: what a reader is shown of it before revealing anything, with ▮ for each spoiler. hidden: what each spoiler hides, in order. Both are the text alone, markup taken off, with ⌷ for each code span or block, a space for anything else that is not text (a line break, HTML), a line break after whatever is not in a line of text (a paragraph, a heading, a table cell), and each run of spaces, tabs, and line breaks read as one space and none at either end.",
